## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`getSingleEntry`): This is the Contentstack SDK integration layer where content is fetched. Live Preview requires passing preview parameters to the Contentstack SDK Stack initialization and query calls. The function signature (confirmed at line 236) accepts contentTypeUid, entryUid, lang, referenceFieldPath, jsonRtePath, only, except — but no preview/draft parameter. The Stack object (confirmed exported from this file via test imports) also lacks live_preview config. This is the CAUSE: the data-fetching layer never requests draft/preview content from Contentstack, so the CMS can never show live previews regardless of what the presentation layer does.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add live_preview configuration to the Contentstack Stack initialization (the Stack object exported from this file) with { host, enable: true } per Contentstack SDK docs. Then add an optional preview parameter (e.g. live_preview?: { enable: boolean; content_type_uid?: string; entry_uid?: string }) to IContentstackGetSingleEntry and to getEntry/getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry. When preview is enabled, call .includeFallback() on the query chain (Contentstack SDK method for live preview drafts). In each page's getStaticProps, pass context.preview and context.previewData through to these service calls so draft content is fetched when the CMS requests it.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- When a content editor makes a change in the CMS and it, the change appears in the preview view of the page without the page performing a full reload
- When a page is opened from the Contentstack preview (e.g. by clicking preview in the CMS), the rendered page shows the latest saved draft edits, including content not yet published
- When the same page is opened normally outside preview mode (e.g. via its public URL), the rendered page shows the published version of the content, not unpublished draft edits
- When a card's title, description, link, or image is edited in the CMS, the corresponding change is observable on that card as rendered on the previewed page
- When a link, image, or table in the page content is edited in the CMS, the corresponding change is observable in the rendered links, images, and tables on the previewed page
- During a single preview session, multiple successive content edits made in the CMS each appear in the previewed page in turn without requiring the page to be manually refreshed
- When preview updates stop arriving (e.g. the preview connection drops), the page continues to display the most recently shown content without errors or a blank screen
- Draft edits viewed during a preview session never appear on the live published site until the content is actually published in the CMS

